<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mariano Paredes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1797">1797</a>–<a href="/years/1849">1849</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Mariano Paredes y Arrillaga</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mariano Paredes y Arrillaga was a Mexican general and conservative who seized power in a coup in January 1846 and became president. His government refused to negotiate with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexican-american-war">Mexican–American War</a> began during his rule. He was overthrown in August 1846 by a revolt that restored the federal Constitution of 1824.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mariano-paredes.jpg" alt="Mariano Paredes" width="320" height="413" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joaquín Ramírez · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Presidente_Mariano_Paredes_y_Arrillaga.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
